\import{discrete-macros}

\title{The product rule}

\p{The first principle we will consider is the \em{product rule}. Note, instead of just talking about the sizes of sets we will often talk in terms of \em{choosing} elements of a set. The number of elements in a set is the same as the number of ways to choose a different element of the set, so in some sense this makes no difference; but for some reason it is often helpful to think in terms of actively \em{choosing} elements rather than just passively \em{counting} them.}

